{{also|riff-raff}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|riff-raff}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|fro|rif}} {{m|fro|et|}} {{m|fro|raf||one and all}}, of {{der|en|gem|-}} origin.  The first word is from {{m|fro|rifler||to scrape off}} and the last is from {{m|fro|raffler}}, related to {{m|fro|rafler||to plunder}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹɪfɹæf/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# The [[rabble]]; [[crowds]]; the common people.
#: ''They started charging a modest fee in an effort to keep the '''riffraff''' out.''
#* {{quote-video game|en|date=10 December 2019|developer=[[w:Yacht Club Games|Yacht Club Games]]|title=[[w:Shovel Knight: King of Cards|Shovel Knight: King of Cards]]|platform=[[w:Nintendo 3DS|Nintendo 3DS]]|scene=ending|text=''Mom'': [Walks away with King Pridemoor.] / ''King Knight'': 'MOM, WAIT! ..... MOM!! *SIGH* WELL, FINALLY, THE '''RIFF-RAFF'''... AND MY MOM, ARE GONE.'}}
# Sweepings; refuse.

